From 60f793959477424664f04e5f494ba1f06ccbff1e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian MacDonald <ian@netstatz.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 19:02:19 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 043/109] fix(beacon): fail closed on an unknown arrival
 interface; report unmatched allow-list names

With beacon_listen_interfaces set, a beacon whose arrival interface cannot
be learned (no IP_PKTINFO, or its setsockopt failed) is now dropped on every
socket, not only on 255.255.255.255, and counted in stats.unknown_interface.
A failed IP_PKTINFO setsockopt is logged. Without an allow-list nothing
changes.

Allow-list names that match no interface with an RFC1918 address are logged
when the set changes and listed in beacon_listener.unmatched_interfaces;
when none match, listening is false and error names them.

Assisted-by: claude:opus-5.5
